\ Build-cost driver for the colliding `connect` exports in lib/net/tcp.1z
\ and lib/net/tls.1z. Per-module compiled word identity makes an AOT build
\ compile both modules' bodies instead of one bare-name winner. The driver
\ is only ever AOT-built by benchmark-collision-build and is excluded from
\ `make benchmark`, since running it would dial live endpoints.

net: "net" load ;
tcp: "net/tcp" load ;
tls: "net/tls" load ;

"127.0.0.1" 9 net.make-addr:tcp tcp.connect drop
"localhost" 9 tls.connect drop
